<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Flowchart depicting a brain-computer interface system. On the left, "Data Preparation" involves recording EEG signals from subjects. The "Processing Unit" includes preprocessing, feature extraction, and statistical analysis. The classification stage follows, leading to commands for "External Devices" in the "Feedback" section. Stimulus or instruction initiates the process.) /K 1808 0 R /P 273 0 R /Pg 247 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
1744 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Flowchart outlining a review focused on EEG analysis and identification of Alzheimer's disease. It includes sections like background, theme, and body. Under AD Analysis Methods, components listed are participant background, channels, experimental protocol, characteristic form, and analytical methods. Discussion of results covers EEG biomarkers, brain regions, model analysis, and other biomarkers. Conclusion and trends lead to a vision emphasizing accurate diagnosis to alleviate social burden.) /K 1809 0 R /P 273 0 R /Pg 248 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
1745 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Flowchart outlining a research process. Websites used are Scholar Google and PubMed, with time limitations from 2018 to 2025. Queries focus on EEG, electroencephalography, and Alzheimer's Disease. Screening removes specific types of articles, leading to inclusion of 100 articles for LC-I and 41 for LC-II.) /K 1810 0 R /P 273 0 R /Pg 248 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
1746 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Line graph showing percentage versus number of datasets. Two series are highlighted: blue circles for males and red stars for females, across two sections labeled LC-I and LC-II. The data points fluctuate between 0 to 100 percent.) /K 1811 0 R /P 273 0 R /Pg 250 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
1747 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Scatter plots display the number of subjects in two comparisons: left, with two classes and right, with three classes. Data is clustered into specified ranges, using gradients from dark blue to light yellow to indicate varying subject numbers within each class.) /K 1812 0 R /P 273 0 R /Pg 251 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
1748 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Scatter plots showing the distribution of subjects in two classes and three classes. The left plot shows a linear increase in the number of subjects across four ranges. The right plot displays a similar distribution in three classes with varied distribution across three ranges, showing more clustered and dispersed points at higher subject numbers.) /K 1813 0 R /P 273 0 R /Pg 252 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
